Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "country_code": country indicator ⇒ filter to 'US' only  
• "kind_code": publication kind ⇒ filter to 'B2' (granted utility patents)  
• "grant_date": numeric yyyymmdd ⇒ filter between 20220601 and 20220831 (Jun‑Aug 2022)  
• "application_kind": broad patent type ⇒ optional extra screen for utility patents ('A' or blank)  
• "ipc": VARIANT array with objects that contain a "code" key ⇒ flatten to pull every IPC code attached to a publication  
• "publication_number": publication identifier ⇒ keep for inspection / grouping  

Typical WHERE‑clause conditions that may be used  
• "country_code" = 'US'  
• "kind_code" = 'B2'  
• "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831  
• Optional: "application_kind" = 'A'  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (LIMIT 20 each) that move from very simple inspections toward the final aggregation needed.  
All column names are wrapped in double quotes as required.  

```sql
-- Description: Quick look at 2022 grants to confirm date format and counts
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "cnt_2022_grants"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220101 AND 20221231
  AND "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Show a few rows of US B2 patents granted in June‑Aug 2022
SELECT "publication_number", "grant_date", "kind_code", "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Inspect the raw structure of the "ipc" variant column
SELECT "publication_number",
       "ipc"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Flatten the IPC array and list one IPC per row for sample patents
SELECT t."publication_number",
       f.value:"code"::STRING AS "ipc_code_full"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Extract the 4‑digit IPC (first four characters) for inspection
SELECT DISTINCT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count occurrences of each 4‑digit IPC among June‑Aug‑2022 US B2 grants
SELECT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
       COUNT(*) AS "ipc4_count"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY "ipc4_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Same as above but only use IPC entries marked as main ("first" = true) when present
SELECT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
       COUNT(*) AS "ipc4_count"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
  AND (f.value:"first" IS NULL OR f.value:"first"::BOOLEAN)   -- keep main or only entry
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY "ipc4_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: List the 4‑digit IPC together with sample publication numbers (showing 2 per IPC)
SELECT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
       t."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4)
                           ORDER BY t."publication_number") <= 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Verify that adding application_kind='A' (utility) does not change IPC ordering
SELECT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
       COUNT(*) AS "ipc4_count"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY "ipc4_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Final aggregation to return only the single most frequent 4‑digit IPC code
SELECT SUBSTR(f.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."ipc") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

